{"id":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3#def:complete-integral","title":"def:complete-integral","path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.md","line":19,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex#def:complete-integral","uses":[],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Evans/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter3.tex","label":"def:complete-integral","line":15,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Complete integral]\n\\label{def:complete-integral}\n\\dcref{ch3:3.1.1-def-1}\n\\group{Nonlinear First-Order PDE}\nA family $u=u(x,a)$, $a\\in\\R^n$, is a complete integral of\n$F(Du,u,x)=0$ if every $u(\\cdot,a)$ is a solution and\n\\[\n\\operatorname{rank}\n\\begin{pmatrix}D_a u\\\\D^2_{xa}u\\end{pmatrix}=n.\n\\]\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Complete integral] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a636f6d706c6574652d696e74656772616c\"></span> <span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch3:3.1.1-def-1</span></span>\\group Nonlinear First-Order PDE A family <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u=u(x,a)$\">$u=u(x,a)$</span>, <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$a\\in \\R ^n$\">$a\\in \\R ^n$</span>, is a complete integral of <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$F(Du,u,x)=0$\">$F(Du,u,x)=0$</span> if every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$u(\\cdot ,a)$\">$u(\\cdot ,a)$</span> is a solution and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"true\" data-tex=\"\\[  \\operatorname {rank} \\begin{pmatrix} D_a u\n\n\\\\ D^2_{xa}u\n\n\\end{pmatrix}=n.  \\]\">\\[  \\operatorname {rank} \\begin{pmatrix} D_a u\n\n\\\\ D^2_{xa}u\n\n\\end{pmatrix}=n.  \\]</span> ","warnin